+# Solution
+
+`redact` processes the input line by line while preserving the original line endings. Lines whose first token starts with `DEBUG_` are returned unchanged. On every other line, a compiled case-insensitive regular expression replaces each word-boundary-delimited `key-`, `sk-`, or `tok_` value with at least 12 alphanumeric characters with `***`.
+
+The specification says masking is “unconditional across the entire input,” but then gives an explicit operational exception for `DEBUG_` logger lines. The implementation treats that later, more specific exception as authoritative.
+
+Verification: `python3 -m pytest -q` passes all tests.
